# Project Conventions

When implementing features or making changes:

- **Assistant language:** [.cursor/rules/communication-language.mdc](.cursor/rules/communication-language.mdc) — reply in the same language the user writes; offer clearer English when they ask.
- Follow [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) for tech stack and module layout.
- **Architecture doc maintenance:** After meaningful changes, update [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) in the same change set when the overview would be wrong or incomplete — e.g. new/removed Nest modules or controllers, Prisma models or major fields, auth or realtime behavior, main frontend routes, observability/OpenAPI workflow, or tech stack. Skip edits for trivial fixes that do not alter the documented system shape.
- **Backend API:** [.cursor/rules/api-database-consistency.mdc](.cursor/rules/api-database-consistency.mdc) — persist to PostgreSQL via Prisma; no mock data for persisted entities.
- **Frontend UI:** [.cursor/rules/ui-styles.mdc](.cursor/rules/ui-styles.mdc) — theme-aware classes (`group-data-[theme=light]`).
- **Automated tests:** [.cursor/rules/no-unrequested-tests.mdc](.cursor/rules/no-unrequested-tests.mdc) — do not add or extend tests unless the user explicitly asks.
- **Test scenarios (when you write or edit tests):** [.cursor/rules/test-scenario-conventions.mdc](.cursor/rules/test-scenario-conventions.mdc) — data-driven / matrix naming, optional QA tags (`[Boundary]`, `[Stress]`, etc.) only when accurate; applies under `tests/` for any test type.
- **Playwright UI tests (when you write them):** [.cursor/rules/playwright-ui-tests.mdc](.cursor/rules/playwright-ui-tests.mdc) — `toHaveURL` path strings when `baseURL` is set; RegExp when matching is partial or flexible; use `tag` (`@smoke`, `@merge-gate`, `@client-validation`, etc.). Matrix row names also follow `test-scenario-conventions.mdc`.
- **Feature branches:** use `feature/<short-description>`; do not commit directly to `main` / `master`.
- **One active feature at a time:** do **not** create a new `feature/*` branch **from** another `feature/*` branch, and do **not** stack a second feature branch on top of in-progress work. If the repo is already on a `feature/*` branch for one piece of work, either (1) finish, PR, and merge that branch to `master` **before** starting a new feature branch from `master`, or (2) if the user asks for additional work that is a **different** functionality, **ask them** whether to extend the **current** branch or wait until the current feature is merged—do not silently mix unrelated features or branch off the current feature branch without their decision.
- **GitHub:** [.cursor/rules/github-pr-workflow.mdc](.cursor/rules/github-pr-workflow.mdc) — open PR to `master` (`gh` or REST API + `GITHUB_TOKEN` from `.env`); **merge on GitHub only** after explicit merge approval; never substitute a local merge to `master` for a PR unless the user explicitly asks.
- Prefer small, focused changes; avoid unrelated refactors.
